                <pb facs="0272" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 294/148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Herrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-26T11:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 26,
                                1923—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 26—9:22
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>147. W–12. How low a rate of interest would you accept if you approve in
                    principle of the plan for limiting loss by having the deficits carry interest to
                    establish the basis of 12 annual installments? <pb facs="0273" n="149"
                        xml:id="pg149"/> It is my suggestion that 4% would not appear to be too low
                    and that we might even make it somewhat less. Wadsworth.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
